From: Riaz <riaz@riazcomputer.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:24:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Student list: card -> list layout; add NCTB-based subject
 requirement seeder

1) Office > Students: replace the card-grid layout with a proper
   table/list view (checkbox, ID, name, class, roll, gender, status,
   actions). All existing per-row actions (Edit, Details, Test/
   Marksheet, ID Card, Issue TC, Discontinue, Certificates, SSC,
   Delete) and duplicate-highlighting are preserved, just rendered as
   table rows instead of cards. The print view is unchanged.

2) New management command 'seed_subject_requirements': auto-populates
   SubjectRequirement rows for class 9-10 based on the standard NCTB
   SSC group structure (Science / Business Studies / Humanities) --
   compulsory subjects (Bangla, English, ICT, BGS, etc.), a
   religion-conditional subject, and group-specific mandatory +
   optional (4th subject / elective) subjects. Run with
   'python manage.py seed_subjects' first to load the Subject master
   list, then 'python manage.py seed_subject_requirements' (optional
   --institution <id> to scope to one institution). Existing rows are
   left untouched, so it's safe to re-run, and everything it creates
   can still be edited/deleted from the existing Subject Requirements
   page -- institutions are free to adjust to their own board/syllabus.

   NOTE: this is a reasonable reference structure, not an official
   NCTB document -- please spot-check the seeded subjects against your
   institution's actual syllabus and edit/delete rows as needed.

Verified via Django test client + full test suite. Two pre-existing
test failures (test_promotion_requires_session_and_records_history,
test_selected_institution_filters_student_list) predate this commit
-- confirmed by testing against the prior commit -- and are unrelated
to these changes; likely worth a look separately.
